# name: test/sql/cityjson_hollow_solid.test
# description: a hollow Solid (interior shell) read from CityJSON through three_d
# group: [sql]

# End-to-end of the design-doc §7 composition for the capability this stack
# exists to serve: computing the volume of a solid with an interior shell
# (a cavity), where the shell partition the WKB flattens away is recovered from
# the spec §8 `geometry_properties` `shells` key.
#
# Fixture: test/data/hollow_solid.city.json — outer cube [0,4]^3 (V=64) with a
# concentric cavity [1,3]^3 (V=8), the cavity wound opposite the exterior.
# Hollow volume = 64 - 8 = 56.
#
# The `cityjson` build must be the sibling duckdb-cityjson checkout: it emits the
# per-LoD `geometry_lod<X>` / `geometry_properties_lod<X>` pair, with `shells` in
# the CityParquet `List<List<Int32>>` shape ([[6, 6]] for a two-shell Solid).
# `require cityjson` skips this test when it is not staged for the runner; see
# docs/CITYJSON_INTEROP.md.
#
# The metadata path recovers the two shells and the winding check applies. The
# volume would be 56 even from a single merged shell — signed-volume subtraction
# is shell-grouping invariant for a disjoint cavity (DESIGN_DOC §8.2) — so the
# shell count is asserted alongside it, and the shells-driven path and winding
# enforcement are pinned CI-independently by test/sql/st_3d_hollow_solid.test
# and test/cpp/test_inner_shell.cpp.
#
# Note the LoD suffix is the NORMALISED LoD: `lod => '2'` yields `_lod2_0`.
require cityjson

require three_d

# The sidecar carries the per-shell face counts, nested one level.
query II
SELECT geometry_properties_lod2_0.type, geometry_properties_lod2_0.shells
FROM read_cityjson('test/data/hollow_solid.city.json', lod => '2')
WHERE geometry_lod2_0 IS NOT NULL;
----
Solid	[[6, 6]]

# Two shells recovered, hollow volume 56, and the solid is closed.
query III
SELECT ST_3DNumShells(s), ROUND(ST_3DVolume(s), 6), ST_3DIsClosed(s)
FROM (
    SELECT ST_3DFromWKB(geometry_lod2_0, geometry_properties_lod2_0) AS s
    FROM read_cityjson('test/data/hollow_solid.city.json', lod => '2')
    WHERE geometry_lod2_0 IS NOT NULL
) q;
----
2	56.0	true
